# (build 142) The portraits drawn from their pictures (assets/art/portraits,
# docs/asset_format.md): each portrait window's interior takes its colours
# from the picture tools/extract_pictures.py made of its tiles, map and
# palette, and its indices from the tiles as before (video.c's
# VideoPicture; the proof that the two are the same is
# tools/colour_check.py over every route). `expect picture X Y THING` says
# which picture a pixel's colour came from.
#
# The Governor at the start of the game (portrait 23, line 2), then the
# walk home and Rolf's house: Rolf's own window (his art at $4A0, line 1,
# which BuildingScreen loads there), and Nei's portrait arriving mid-scene
# (LoadPortraits' art at $400, line 2). Fails on b141d: the probe has no
# `expect picture`, and nothing was drawn from a picture.

start building 14 23 0 0 32 16      # the Governor; the street is 32,16
wait idle
expect picture 125 60 governor
expect picture 40 40 none           # the room: black, no window
shot 01_governor
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait screen level                   # Demo_TowerToHouse
wait screen building
wait idle
expect picture 258 70 rolf
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle                           # "Nei, I have to leave for awhile..."
expect picture 60 80 nei
expect picture 258 70 rolf
shot 02_house_nei
